# CANDIDATE NOTE (direction constraint)
{{ note }}
The note is the candidate's own adjustment direction: when it conflicts with the question metadata above, follow the note. The note must never make you output essay text.
{% endif %}

# RED LINES
- This task performs NO retrieval and has NO notebook context and NO model essay text: the only input is the exam metadata above plus the candidate's own note.
- NEVER reproduce or paraphrase any 范文 (model essay) passage. "Material match" describes which kinds of candidate project experiences tend to support an angle — never any specific article.
- Angle names and thesis hints are demonstrations to choose from: the final thesis sentence 必须由考生自己改写定稿 (must be rewritten and finalized by the candidate).

# OUTPUT — JSON with two keys
1. angles: exactly 4-6 candidate argument angles. For each angle:
   - name: the angle in one line (标题式短语，点明技术主张).
   - thesis_hint: one-sentence direction for the thesis statement (主旨候选句方向，一句).
   - material_match: 高/中/低 + one sentence on what kind of candidate project material tends to support this angle.
   - difficulty: "easy" | "medium" | "hard" — how costly it is to organize supporting material (交锋难度，素材组织成本).
   - similarity_risk: "low" | "medium" | "high" — how many candidates will likely pick the same angle; common/大众 angles MUST be marked "high".
2. combo_advice: which 2 angles to pick, why this pairing wins, and how they echo the abstract (摘要) and project background (背景) — concrete, not generic.

Constraints:
- Cover distinct technical postures across the 4-6 angles (不要 4-6 个同质角度); include at least one less-common angle worth the extra effort.
- Write field values in Chinese (enum values stay English).
- Output ONLY the JSON object — no preamble, no markdown fences.

